CAUTION — PyMuPDF is AGPL-3.0. Linking it into a network-served backend can
oblige this project to offer that backend's complete corresponding source under
the AGPL. agrilok is open source, so this is survivable, but it is a real
constraint on anyone who forks this privately. If that is a problem for your
deployment, use pdfplumber or pypdfium2 instead; the extraction interface is
designed to allow that substitution. This trade-off is recorded in
docs/adr/0002-text-layer-before-ocr.md.

